oes each shia person have a connected imam from the 12 imams


No individual Shia person has a personal, uniquely assigned individual Imam from the Twelve Imams. Instead, all Twelver Shia Muslims share the exact same Twelve Imams collectively as their historical, spiritual, and divine guides. [1, 2, 3]
The Role of the Imams
The Twelve Imams are the specific, sequential spiritual and political successors to the Prophet Muhammad.
They are infallible leaders starting with Ali ibn Abi Talib and ending with Muhammad al-Mahdi.
Every Shia Muslim looks to this same single lineage for religious law, Quranic interpretation, and spiritual guidance. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
The Living Connection Today
The twelfth and final leader, Imam Muhammad al-Mahdi, is believed to be currently alive but in a state of occultation (hidden from the physical world) by divine will. [1]
He serves as the single living Imam and spiritual presence for all contemporary Shia Muslims—often described metaphorically as a sun hidden behind clouds—rather than each person having a separate or private Imam. [1, 2]
