The deep eschatological mechanics of the Raj’at (The Return) reveal a profound transition for humanity. During this era, mankind will completely move beyond the physical constraints we know today, eventually expanding into the cosmos. [1, 2]
1. Who Returns on the Side of Good?
The side of absolute good will feature a massive resurrection of the most righteous souls across human history: [1, 2]
The Prophets and Messengers: Major figures like Prophet Adam, Noah, Abraham, Moses, and Jesus will return to finally see the absolute completion of the divine mission on Earth. [1, 2]
The 12 Imams and Ahl al-Bayt: The entire lineage returns to govern. [1]
The Elite Companions: Legendary figures of immense faith—such as Salman al-Farsi, Abu Dharr, Malik al-Ashtar, and the martyrs of Karbala—will be resurrected as the military and political commanders of the Imams. [1, 2]
The Pure Believers: Regular historical people who reached the absolute peak of true faith and sincerely desired to see the reign of justice. [1, 2]
2. How Can We Return?
A Shia Muslim does not have to be a historic saint to return; the doorway to Raj'at is opened through sincere intention (Niyyah) and dedicated prayer during one's lifetime. [1]
Dua al-Ahad: Reciting this specific prayer for 40 consecutive mornings is spiritually promised to record a believer among the helpers of the 12th Imam. The narration states that if you die before his arrival, God will raise you from your grave to serve him. []
Ziyarat Ashura & Ziyarat al-Jamia: Consistently reciting these visitation prayers with the conscious plea, "May God place me among those who take vengeance alongside the guided leader," imprints the soul into the cosmic roll call of the Raj'at. [1, 2]
3. How Long Will the Imams Rule?
The era of the Raj'at is not a brief event; it is an incredibly vast epoch spanning thousands of years. [1]
Imam Hussain’s Long Reign: Hadiths state Imam Hussain will rule for a massive duration—some narrations describe it as lasting so long that his eyebrows will sag over his eyes from old age.
Slowing of Time: Islamic traditions note that during this golden era, cosmic physics will shift. God will command the celestial bodies to slow down. A single year during the Raj'at will feel equivalent to 10 or more of our current years, mathematically extending the Imams' governance across centuries. [1, 2, 3]
4. Transitioning to a Space-Faring Race
The physical and technological reality of humanity will experience a complete metamorphosis. Humanity will absolutely become a space-faring civilization. [1, 2]
In a highly famous narration from Imam al-Baqir regarding the 12th Imam and the subsequent Raj'at, it is stated:
"As for him (the Mahdi), he will be given power over the causes/means... and he will ascend the seven heavens and the seven earths."
The deep theological implications of this text outline how space travel and advanced physics will function:
The Elimination of Technological Limits: The Imams will unlock the remaining 25 "letters" of universal knowledge (humanity currently only operates on 2). This includes mastering gravity, cosmic energy, and travel mechanics that make modern aerospace engineering look primitive.
Unlocking the "Seven Earths": In Shia cosmology, the universe contains other realms and habitable planets ("seven earths"). The veil between Earth and these deep cosmic realms will be lifted. Under the governance of the Imams, righteous humanity will colonize, travel to, and administer these distant celestial realms.
The Rule of Light: Space travel will not rely on destructive fossil fuels or dangerous nuclear rockets. It will function through the mastery of light, cosmic waves, and spiritual physics (Amr). Space will cease to be a hostile vacuum of death and will instead be opened up as a vast, harmonious extension of God's kingdom. [1]
Ultimately, history transitions from a story of planetary survival to a magnificent cosmic civilization. The physical universe becomes a borderless empire ruled by the light of the Prophet and his family. [1]
