The accounts of senior scholars, mystics (Arifeen), and grand Ayatollahs who have spiritual connections to the unseen realm (Malakut) provide a highly consistent picture regarding the current status of the 12th Imam and how we must adjust our prayers today.
1. The "Updates" on the Companions
A major misconception is that the 12th Imam is waiting around with zero companions. According to the top-tier mystics—such as Ayatollah Muhammad-Taqi Bahjat, Ayatollah Tabataba'i, and Sayyid Ali Qadhi—the 12th Imam is never alone.
The Outer Rings: The Imam is constantly surrounded by concentric circles of hidden servants. The closest ring consists of 30 perpetual companions. If one of these 30 dies, a pure soul from Earth is immediately elevated to take their place. They live anonymous lives, helping humanity and executing the Imam's daily directives.
The Status of the 313: When scholars have asked or received spiritual insights regarding the 313 elite commanders, the consistent message is that the "spots" are being filled and tested in real-time. Ayatollah Bahjat famously hinted that the spiritual standards are so high that a person might reach the level of a commander on a Tuesday but lose their spot by Friday due to a single slip of pride or spiritual complacency. The roster is dynamic and being constantly filtered through the trials of the modern world.
2. The Nature of the Modern Companions
Scholars emphasize that the people who qualify for these roles today possess a specific psychological and spiritual profile. They are not monks isolated in caves; they are hyper-functional individuals living in our current era:
Spiritual Fortresses: They are completely immune to the "Dajjalic" system of hyper-consumerism and degenerate media. They can navigate modern society without absorbing its spiritual pollution.
The "Iron Hearts": Narrations and spiritual visions describe them as people who have completely conquered fear. They do not experience anxiety about the future or economic collapse because their trust in God is a tangible reality, not just a concept.
Absolute Obedience: Their loyalty to the Imam of the Time is absolute. Mystics note that if the Imam commanded them to step into a fire, they would do so without a microsecond of intellectual hesitation.
3. How to Weaponize Your Prayers and Namaz
Ayatollah Bahjat and other grand masters left explicit instructions on how a believer must transform their daily rituals from passive habits into active, metaphysical weapons to accelerate the end of the occultation.
Turn Your Namaz (Salat) into a Psychic Beacon
The Focused Boundary: During prayer, your mind cannot wander. Mystics teach that a wandering mind leaks spiritual energy, rendering the prayer useless on the cosmic stage. To weaponize it, you must treat your prayer mat as a literal military outpost where you are reporting for duty to the 12th Imam.
The Sajjada Witness: In your final Sajdah (prostration) of every prayer, before you give your final salutations, you should explicitly invoke the Imam. Scholars recommend making your personal, silent Niyyah (intention): "O Allah, let the spiritual light generated from this Namaz be added to the treasury of the Imam of the Time."
Weaponizing Daily Supplications
The "Emergency" Mindset: Ayatollah Bahjat famously said that Shias pray for the Reappearance of the Imam the way someone asks for rain during a mild dry spell, whereas we should be praying like a passenger trapped on a sinking ship crying out for air.
Targeted Al-Ahad and Al-Faraj: When you recite Dua al-Faraj ("Ilahi ‘azuma’l bala’"), you must visualize the structural oppression across the entire planet. Consciously direct the sound waves and spiritual frequency of your recitation to pierce the hidden realms, pleading with Allah to remove the obstacles facing the Imam.
The Night Prayer (Salat al-Layl): This is the ultimate weapon. Scholars state that it is impossible to be among the elite companions of the Imam without waking up before dawn for Salat al-Layl. The energy generated in the absolute darkness of the night, when the rest of the world is asleep or engaging in sin, is what hardens the soul into the "iron" required to withstand the coming trials of the Sufyani.
