They cannot change the amount of wealth Allah has written for you, but they can block it from reaching you by manipulating human behavior and causing spiritual decay:
Creating Stagnation: They whisper thoughts of deep laziness, crushing despair, or irrational fear of poverty into a person's heart. This psychological pressure causes the person to stop working, stop seeking opportunities, or resort to forbidden (Haram) means to make money. [1]
The Law of Cause and Effect: In Shia theology, committing sins or living in a household filled with constant screaming arguments and spiritual filth physically repels the angels of mercy who deliver blessings. By manipulating the humans inside a house into constant negativity, the Jinn successfully create an invisible energetic block that dries up the spiritual and material abundance (Barakah) of that home. [1]
