wheres this from ? and whats the seal of solomon in shia traditions ? not dumb jewish kaballah and satanism



The formula we discussed belongs to the legacy of Islamic exorcism (Ruqyah) and protective declarations recorded by classical Shia scholars. You can find variations of these commands in foundational texts on spiritual defense, such as Ayatollah Muhammad Baqir Majlisi's masterwork Bihar al-Anwar (specifically the volumes covering the physics of Jinn, medicine, and spiritual remedies) and the protective compilations of Mafatih al-Jinan. [1, 2]
The reference to the Seal of Solomon (Khatam Sulayman) in Shia traditions is entirely distinct from its depiction in Western occultism or Kabbalistic lore. It has no connection to modern pentagrams, hexagrams, or satanic symbols. In authentic Shia theology, the Seal is a metaphysical relic of divine authority. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
1. The True Nature of the Seal in Shia Hadiths
In Twelver Shia texts—such as Basa'ir al-Darajat by Al-Saffar—the Seal of Solomon is a literal, divinely forged ring (Khatam) passed down through the lineage of prophets. [1]
The Inscription: Shia traditions state that the ring was not engraved with geometric shapes or occult signs. It was inscribed with the Greatest Name of God (Al-Ism al-A'zam) and declarations of monotheism (Tawhid). [1, 2]
The Source of Command: The ring itself possessed no magical power. It was a physical token of a divine covenant. When Prophet Sulayman wore it, Allah subjected the winds, animals, and both the righteous and demonic Jinn to his direct command as a prophet. [1, 2, 3]
2. The Twin Metals: Managing the Unseen
According to Shia historical narrations regarding the prophets, Sulayman’s ring was synthesized from two distinct, divinely provided elements to manage the visible and invisible worlds: [1]
The Brass Segment: Used to stamp commands, blessings, and assignments to the faithful, righteous Jinn.
The Iron Segment: Used to issue decrees of binding, confinement, and subdual to the rebellious, predatory Jinn and Shayateen (demons). [1, 2]
3. The Current Location of the Seal
The most crucial theological point regarding the Seal of Solomon in Shia Islam is its relationship to the Ahl al-Bayt and the Imam of the Time: [1]
